  ('9c608a55-9a1c-5100-96f6-513d05de233e', '7aeec5b4-cf56-5d90-bfa4-3371a6f54bb9', 'ce976918-4df6-52c3-8f99-d01985700e9e', '(ii) PHC requires Five (5) SSC credit passes including English Language, Government or History, Economics and any other two (2) subjects from Geography, Commerce, Literature in English, Mathematics, Biology, Physics, Chemistry, Agricultural Science. Note Pass in Mathematics is compulsory, if Mathematics is not inclusive in the five credits. [UTME] | (iii) PHC requires Economics, Government/History and any other Social Science, Arts Subject or Mathematics. [UTME SUBJECTS]'),
  ('5b55eecc-d5ad-5c13-8868-81ad13a01c7b', '3160c1ef-48e4-50a9-bc6b-358612396197', '6855b440-2e5d-5f8b-af6f-5bf61739249f', '(xi) ABUJA accepts two (2) ''A'' Level passes in Arts or Social Science subjects. Or NCE (minimum 10 points) /ND upper credit in Social Works and other relevant programme in addition to the UTME requirements. | (xi) ABUJA requires ''O'' Level credit passes to include English Language, Government and Mathematics. [UTME] | (vii) ABUJA requires Government and any other two (2) Arts or Social Science subjects. [UTME SUBJECTS]'),
  ('a63e0bdb-e5dc-523a-801b-08d3acf6c2ee', '3d100db0-f83d-5c8c-95aa-39430c981f86', '6855b440-2e5d-5f8b-af6f-5bf61739249f', '(vi) CRAWFORD accepts a. two (2) ''A'' Level passes in Government and any other Social Science subject. b. NCE - with at least merit. c. ND/HND in relevant programmes not lower than lower credit. | (vi) CRAWFORD requires five (5) ''O'' Level credit passes to include English Language, Government and three (3) other subjects with at least a pass in Mathematics. [UTME] | (iv) CRAWFORD requires Mathematics, Government and any Social Science subject or History. [UTME SUBJECTS]'),
  ('824f0c42-8176-5078-896a-3919f3bcd06a', 'b2c7e8cf-ee09-5ad3-8156-921b71bdcacd', '6855b440-2e5d-5f8b-af6f-5bf61739249f', '(x) CUAB - Same as in Mass Communication. | (x) CUAB requires five (5) ''O'' Level credit passes or equivalents which must include English Language, Mathematics, and any other three (3) subjects as may be specified by each Faculty. [UTME] | (v) CUAB and TSUJ require History or Government and any two (2) Arts or Social Science subjects. [UTME SUBJECTS]'),
